prompt:
Draw the TEXTURE SHEET itself -- not a character. The picture must be one flat square image that IS a 64 by 64 player skin file for a blocky voxel game, drawn as crisp pixel art and blown up large so every texel is a clean square of flat colour. It must look like a texture atlas: a scatter of small rectangular patches of colour sitting on an empty dark background, the way a skin file looks when you open it in an image editor. Do NOT draw a character standing up, do NOT draw a portrait, and do NOT draw a preview of the model.
This is the layout the game reads, given as texel rectangles [x0, y0, x1, y1] on the 64 by 64 sheet, with x measured from the left edge and y measured DOWN from the top edge:
{"texture": [64, 64], "parts": {"head": {"front": [8,8,16,16], "back": [24,8,32,16], "right": [0,8,8,16], "left": [16,8,24,16], "top": [8,0,16,8], "bottom": [16,0,24,8]}, "hat_outer_layer": {"front": [40,8,48,16], "back": [56,8,64,16], "right": [32,8,40,16], "left": [48,8,56,16], "top": [40,0,48,8], "bottom": [48,0,56,8]}, "body": {"front": [20,20,28,32], "back": [32,20,40,32], "right": [16,20,20,32], "left": [28,20,32,32], "top": [20,16,28,20], "bottom": [28,16,36,20]}, "right_arm": {"front": [44,20,48,32], "back": [52,20,56,32], "right": [40,20,44,32], "left": [48,20,52,32], "top": [44,16,48,20], "bottom": [48,16,52,20]}, "left_arm": {"front": [36,52,40,64], "back": [44,52,48,64], "right": [32,52,36,64], "left": [40,52,44,64], "top": [36,48,40,52], "bottom": [40,48,44,52]}, "right_leg": {"front": [4,20,8,32], "back": [12,20,16,32], "right": [0,20,4,32], "left": [8,20,12,32], "top": [4,16,8,20], "bottom": [8,16,12,20]}, "left_leg": {"front": [20,52,24,64], "back": [28,52,32,64], "right": [16,52,20,64], "left": [24,52,28,64], "top": [20,48,24,52], "bottom": [24,48,28,52]}}}
Every one of those rectangles must be filled in on the sheet, and everything outside them left as empty background. Note that the sheet is NOT a picture of the body: the six faces of one body part are scattered around the sheet, the left arm's rectangles sit far away from the right arm's, and the second 'hat' layer of the head is a separate set of rectangles from the head itself.
DESIGN BRIEF for this character, to be painted into the correct rectangles:
  - the jacket is RED: fill the body rectangles and both arms' rectangles with red;
  - the LEFT ARM has a WHITE STRIPE running the whole way down the front of the sleeve -- and the RIGHT ARM has no stripe at all, it is plain red;
  - the face has GREEN EYES: two green texels on the head's front rectangle;
  - the outer HAT layer is BLUE: fill the hat_outer_layer rectangles with blue;
  - the legs are dark blue trousers.
Flat colours, hard pixel edges, no shading gradients, no words, no letters, no numbers, no grid lines and no labels anywhere in the picture.
